# Steam Deck packages that are NEVER BUNDLED -- fetched over the network at
# install time by configure_deck (T5-fork-plan.md §4.1).
#
# Nothing in this file goes into the offline mirror or into any install list.
# It exists so that ONE build-time check can still ask about them:
# deck-nvidia-dry-run.sh resolves `<what the ISO installs> + <this file>`
# against the online repos, because docs/PROGRESS.md §3.8's failure is a
# property of that combined resolution and of nothing the ISO carries. Leaving
# these out of the question would make the guard green for the wrong reason.
#
# ⚠️ Adding a package here does NOT make it available offline. If a package
# needs to be installable without a network it belongs in
# deck-mirror.packages -- and then its licence has to permit redistribution,
# which is the whole reason these two are here instead.

# Licenses: Proprietary, with no licence text shipped
# (docs/findings/P16-redistribution-and-trademark.md §1). Bundling it into the
# offline mirror would redistribute it; fetching it from Valve's own mirror at
# install time does not. §4.1 decided fetch, not bundle.
steamdeck-dsp

# Steam Subscriber Agreement, and it is huge. Installers normally fetch it.
# It is also the package that makes §3.8 fire at all: `steam` is what depends
# on the virtual vulkan-driver / lib32-vulkan-driver that pacman would
# otherwise satisfy with the NVIDIA stack.
steam
